00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.460
I want you to think about the teacher that
you still today remember.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.759
Think about that one teacher.

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:10.580
We all got one of them, minimum, that we remember,
right?

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.990
Today I'm going to share with you how you
can be that teacher to many people in business

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.990
or in life.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.180
Because in reality, as an entrepreneur, one
of the things you'll do a lot is teaching.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.490
You'll teach your clients.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.840
You'll teach your vendors.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.080
You'll teach your partners about your company,
and investors.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.140
You'll teach your salespeople, you'll teach
everybody about who you are and what you do.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.840
And the better you are at teaching, the better
your business is going to do, and the more

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.879
you're going to grow because everyone's learning
how to take the stuff that you know in here

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:37.879
and implement it.

00:00:37.879 --> 00:00:38.879
So let's get right into it.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.480
Step #1: Whatever you're teaching, sell what
you're teaching.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.660
Let me explain.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.679
If you're teaching me math, sell me the importance
of wanting to learn math.

00:00:48.679 --> 00:00:49.679
Sell me.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:50.679
Sell it to me.

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:51.679
Here's why math is so important!

00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:52.879
It's so exciting.

00:00:52.879 --> 00:00:56.920
And everything in life is math because if
you look at everything, it's angles and sports

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.190
is math and everything is math.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.190
Sell it to me.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.850
Sell me whatever you're teaching, is step
#1.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:02.850
#2.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.740
If you can find a way to add fun, humor and
creativity to it, what you do is this.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.740
This is what happens.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.090
Think about the mind being close-minded.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.970
So the mind is closed.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.810
Every time you use fun, humor, or creativity,
it opens up my mind.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.530
Just think about visually I have a hole here.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.340
When it opens up my mind, I'm willing to have
information enter my mind.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.109
Great teachers know how to have fun, humor,
creativity open up the mind so they're willing

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:31.320
to be sold on whatever you're teaching to
them.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:38.009
And if, IF, you know how to add sticky stories
to whatever you're teaching, using some sort

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:41.630
of fun, humor and creativity, it sticks forever.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:44.330
People will tell those stories forever and
they'll remember whatever you're teaching

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.630
them, based on the story you told because
when they go home at night, you know what

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.630
they're going to tell them?

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.789
Hey, honey, you won't believe what I learned
today.

00:01:49.789 --> 00:01:50.899
What did you learn?

00:01:50.899 --> 00:01:56.320
Did you know that in 1976 Steve Jobs. . . and
because of that, this is how the PC came out

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.359
and the mouse and.

00:01:57.359 --> 00:01:58.740
. . No way, babe!

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.319
You just sold them why they need to learn
this, you added fun, humor and creativity,

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:03.319
you had a sticky story.

00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:06.060
It stuck, they went and taught their wife
and their three kids that night - you're a

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.380
great teacher.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.979
#3, Simplify.

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:09.979
Make it look easy.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:11.120
Whatever you're doing, make it look easy.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.250
Don't complicate things.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.080
Make it look very easy.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.050
#4, Give them steps.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.650
First you do this, then you do that then you
do this.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.180
Give them simple steps to follow that if they
do, they can do what you're teaching them

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.180
to do.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.380
#5: Sell belief.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.380
This is easy.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.380
You can do it.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.380
It's not that hard.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.380
Sell them the belief.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.380
You can pull this off, right?

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:33.080
So if I'm teaching how to shoot a basketball,
step #1, bend your knees.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.780
Two, boom, this is three, it's easy.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.780
You can do it.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.780
Let's do it again.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.780
Let's do it again.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.570
Next, teach the way they learn.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:44.620
Some learn visually, some learn through reading,
some learn through listening.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.210
Some learn through hands on.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:50.240
Teach so many different ways that you can
pretty much teach all the different audiences

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.330
on the way that they learn, whatever you are
trying to teach them.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.850
Next, re-remind.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:59.470
This is typically the biggest mistake teachers
make is because they forget to re-remind,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.470
and re-remind.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.190
They say, "Don't you already get it?

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.610
Haven't I already told you?

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.100
I already told you this!"

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.830
So for me when I go home every night, I ask
both of my sons, "What are the four things

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.670
we focus on as a family.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.340
That we lead, love, respect, improve.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.340
Do we bully?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.340
No.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.340
Do we get bullied?

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.340
No."

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.340
I've probably asked them this two, three hundred
times.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.360
Do you know why?

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.210
Because teaching is about re-reminding.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.930
Not just saying it one time and they remember.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.330
It's about reminding.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.940
Think about it like a commercial.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.890
Toyota does the same commercial, same commercial,
same commercial, same commercial, and then

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:30.890
you say it.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.060
Guinness, you know the drink, does the same
commercial, same commercial, same commercial,

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.060
and then you say it.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.060
Re-remind.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.000
You're like a commercial you're doing to teach
people.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.440
Next, be patient.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.440
Why?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.910
Because the speed of learning varies for everybody.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.910
Some learn fast.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.330
Some don't learn fast.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.100
And sometimes the best students end up being
the ones that don't learn fast.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.810
So can you imagine if you go all in, just
with the guy that learns very fast, but he's

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.830
lazy, then you got a guy here that takes him
six months to learn, but he's the hardest

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.090
working guy you got.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.650
You got to make sure you vary, based on what
speed learning they learn.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.740
And last but not least, be a great student.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:05.300
If you're a great student, typically the greatest
teachers make the greatest students.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:10.060
I don't know why that is, because you're so
curious yourself, you're always learning.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.220
People want to learn from you because this
